{
  "source": "Built for T-0208 (RQ-0185) in the shape of the T-0189 follow-ups fixture (RQ-0173), from the Refund object and RefundListParams of the official stripe@23.1.0 type definitions (Refund.status pending | requires_action | succeeded | failed | canceled). Not recorded from a live account: no Stripe key or network was available. The nightly sweep only lists refunds (GET /v1/refunds by payment_intent); there is deliberately no POST interaction, so any create the sweep or its handler attempted would be answered 400 and listed as a mismatch. 'unapproved': a live (pending) refund for a document nobody approved (review r8 R2). 'unrecorded': a succeeded refund for an approved document with no stripe_refund row (a lost commit). 'cancelled': a succeeded refund for a cancelled document (review r10 M1(c)). 'clean': nothing. 'failedonly': only a failed refund (no money out). 'twice': two live refunds for one document. 'foreign': another tenant's stray.",
